On 2006-07-13, Batman? <fermat111@hotmail.com> wrote:
> anyway, i have a elven short sword, and a long sword, should i
> increase my skill in long sword? i can upgrade axe and short sword
> right now, but i dont want to waste skill slots, expecially on axe,
> which I dont htink is useful.

Even without any artifacts, long swords are better. Any long sword you
choose will better than any short sword in at least the large creature
category. Also, as a barbarian, you can only achieve "basic" skill in
short swords, but you can go to "skilled" in long sword.

> Will I be able to handle the top level of Soko?

You should be fine -- just follow these simple rules:
1) Don't play "let's see who can hit the hardest" with a mumak. The
mumak wins.
2) Don't be burdened. Leocrottas love that.

> Also I havent found any shops yet, it there any other way to ID scrolls
> other than reading them?

Since we're on the topic of Sokoban, the pair of matching scrolls you
found lying on the first level of Sokoban are always scrolls of earth.

> assuming I can fix my mistake.

That's usually not a problem. If you can't fix it by judiciously
squeezing through boulders, make use of those scrolls of earth (that's
what they're there for). IIRC, doing either of those things in Sokoban
is -1 to luck. That honestly won't matter at all in the long run, so
don't worry about it. You're going to have sorry luck anyway until you
get a luckstone.



